ropist, the garden has evolved into one of the foremost botanical research centers in the world, contributing significantly to the understanding and preservation of plant biodiversity. Spanning 79 acres, it houses over 6,000 species of plants, making it an invaluable resource for both scholars and the general public, who seek to understand the complexities of plant life and its ecological significance.

